[Themes "queenside-expansion,good-bishop"]

1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nf3 Bg7 4. g3 O-O 5. Bg2 d6 6. O-O Nc6 { Develops and pressures d4. The knight also prepares ...a6 and ...Rb8. }
7. Nc3 ( 7. d5 Na5 { The knight is on the edge, but it eyes c4, and ...c5 will give it a good home. } 8. Nbd2 c5 9. Qc2 b5 10. cxb5 Nxd5 )
7... a6 { Prepares ...Rb8 and ...b5, a break on the queenside that hits White's c4 pawn. } 8. h3 Rb8 { The rook backs up the coming ...b5. }
9. Be3 Bd7 { Develops the last minor piece and gives the knight on c6 a defender. } 10. Qd2 b5 { The pawn break arrives. Black opens the b-file for the rook and trades off White's c-pawn. [%cal Gb5c4] } 11. cxb5 axb5 *
